    },
    "message": "Move the agent dynamics namespace and the action lifecycle's receipts into Rust\n\nRust owns agent_dynamics_v1 and its writers (rules/agent_dynamics.rs), and writes each lifecycle\nreceipt as an EventRow through EventWriter, with no Python object (rules/action_lifecycle.rs).\nA controller keeps its open actions in ActiveActions; a Python rule gets a plain dict. The row\nkernel replaces agent_dynamics_valid. EventWriter.record now refuses a negative minute as\nEventLogRecord does, and the metrics read the IDs at a minute without making records.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
