    },
    "message": "Leave a rule's counter and a record missing from its tree to Python, before anything is written\n\nA rule adds to the event counter unchecked, and a counter near the end of i64 would have wrapped\nwhere Python's int goes on: EventWriter::of now refuses it, and schedule a sequence whose counter\nwould not fit. A record taken past the tree made the agent dynamics writers raise, or change the row\nand not the tree: they now say Unsupported with the row as it was. What is left to fail inside\ncommit is memory and bugs, not data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
